# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 4 ("the order of a group's lines decides positions and nothing else"), ch. 8 (a clause is chosen by its pattern) and ruling TC (places counted as built): loud gives the inner `if`'s 3, so the widget's clause `k` builds "one 3" and "two 3" at 0 and 1, the `for` its two rows at 2 and 3, the inner arm its label at 4; soft gives 20 and builds nothing in its arm. Never run: prismc refuses the program.
test loud

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Label(text="one 3")
    1: Ui.Label(text="two 3")
    2: Ui.Label(text="row 1")
    3: Ui.Label(text="row 2")
    4: Ui.Label(text="inner")

test soft

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Label(text="one 20")
    1: Ui.Label(text="two 20")
